6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this
License, in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embedded in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium
(including a physical distribution medium) with the object code.

b) Convey the object code in, or embedded in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as
long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that product,
to give anyone who possesses the object code a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
physical distribution medium) at no more than your reasonable cost
of actually performing this service; or, in the case of a physical
product, to give anyone who possesses the object code a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
physical distribution medium) at no more than your reasonable cost
of actually performing this service.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
physical distribution medium) for each recipient, if the distribution
is made in a way that does not give the recipient a persistent
opportunity to compare the copies with the original. The Corresponding
Source must be provided at no more than your reasonable cost of
actually performing this service.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated place
(which may be a server), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
additional charge. You need not offer access to the Corresponding
Source for the same object code if no one accesses the object code
over the network. If the object code is being conveyed in a
distributed computing system, the Corresponding Source should be
provided in a way that is accessible from the network where the
object code is being conveyed. This requirement also applies when
the object code is used to provide a service on a network.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission, provided
you inform other peers of the object code and the Corresponding
Source of the object code is being conveyed in a way that is
consistent with this License.

A separable portion of the object code whose source code is the
source code of a specific User Product is a "User Product" if it is
(a) a consumer product, or (b) anything designed or sold for
incorporation into a dwelling. If the object code is conveyed in a
User Product with a copy of the Corresponding Source, the
Corresponding Source must be included in a way that is included in
the form of a gift, in which case you must also include the
Corresponding Source. You must also include a copy of the
Corresponding Source if the object code is in a User Product and
the distribution is made under section 6b.

